{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_13-42-19-etcd_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nsrc=json.load(open('update3.json'))\ndef chain(a,b): return {\\\"field\\\":\\\"scenario\\\",\\\"reference\\\":b+\\\".scenario\\\"}\nexp={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"9ad1a10e85bb41578fbb8a42a6890ab3-question-0\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_singleton_test.go\\\",\n \\\"previous_id\\\":\\\"9ad1a10e85bb41578fbb8a42a6890ab3-experiment\\\",\n \\\"revision_reason\\\":\\\"The first execution of this basis (CheckRun c39e3b84d6174ce390e9320c9d2bab1b) parsed all six events without loss but returned unknown for all five comparisons, with the diagnostics 'No corresponding prerequisite events reached' and 'No complete applicable result observation': identity_fields used the per-event step value, so no prerequisite event could satisfy the witness identity check. The harness now stamps a shared scenario field on every event, and the prerequisite aliases are correlated through it so that each compared event, its admission alias and the alias chain belong to the same scenario.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"tracker-singleton\\\",\\\"readindex-singleton-branch\\\",\\\"stepleader-decl\\\",\\\"prop-removed-leader\\\",\\\"switchtoconfig-removal\\\",\\\"config-stepdown-doc\\\",\\\"readonlysafe-doc\\\",\\\"node-readindex-contract\\\"],\n \\\"anchors\\\":src['experiment']['anchors'],\n \\\"scope\\\":src['experiment']['scope'],\n \\\"prefix\\\":src['experiment']['prefix'],\n \\\"requirement\\\":src['experiment']['requirement'],\n \\\"responsibility\\\":src['experiment']['responsibility'],\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"setup\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"setup\\\"},\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"removed\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"leader_removed\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[chain(\\\"removed\\\",\\\"setup\\\")]},\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"newlead\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"new_leader_committed\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[chain(\\\"newlead\\\",\\\"removed\\\")]},\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"stale\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"stale_read_answered\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[chain(\\\"stale\\\",\\\"newlead\\\")]},\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"control\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"control_read_actual_leader\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[chain(\\\"control\\\",\\\"stale\\\")]},\n ],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"leader_removed\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"scenario\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"setup\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"state\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"StateLeader\\\"},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"The node whose removal the application applied is still leading, with a configuration whose single voter is another node (singleton true, is_voter false).\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"new_leader_committed\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"scenario\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"removed\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"actual_leader_ahead\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"The actual leader of the reduced configuration has committed an entry that the removed leader's commit index does not cover (committed 4 vs 2).\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"stale_read_answered\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"scenario\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"newlead\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"read_index_at_least_other_committed\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"antecedent\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"read_states\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Witness: the removed leader answered the ReadIndex request with index 2, below the commit index 4 the actual leader already had, without sending any message (heartbeats_emitted 0, messages_emitted empty, pending_reads 0).\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"control_read_actual_leader\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"scenario\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"stale\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"read_index_at_least_own_committed\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: the same request answered by the node that is the actual leader of the configuration returns an index that covers its commit index, so the local singleton answer is only unsafe on the node that is no longer the voter.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"second_stale_read\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"scenario\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"control\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"same_stale_index_as_first\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"No repair from the periodic path: after three heartbeat intervals and no replies from the current configuration, the removed leader is still leading at its old term and still answers with the same stale index.\\\"},\n ],\n}\nu={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The first execution of the removed-singleton-leader probe was inconclusive for a wiring reason, not for the target: all five comparisons returned unknown because identity_fields used a per-event value. This update records that outcome against the question, answers the registered gap from the same receipt's raw events, and resubmits a revised experiment whose harness stamps a shared scenario field and whose prerequisite aliases are correlated through it.\\\",\n \\\"experiment\\\":exp,\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[{\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"9ad1a10e85bb41578fbb8a42a6890ab3-question-0\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"tracker-singleton\\\",\\\"readindex-singleton-branch\\\",\\\"prop-removed-leader\\\",\\\"switchtoconfig-removal\\\",\\\"config-stepdown-doc\\\",\\\"readonlysafe-doc\\\",\\\"node-readindex-contract\\\",\\\"readme-linearizable\\\"],\n  \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"c39e3b84d6174ce390e9320c9d2bab1b\\\":[1,2,3,4,5]},\n  \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"unresolved\\\",\n  \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n  \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The current account of this question is source-grounded and empirically undecided. The source account is unchanged: tracker.IsSingleton (tracker/tracker.go:158-162) tests only the size of the configuration, so stepLeader's MsgReadIndex case (raft.go:1354-1361) answers locally - ReadState for a local request, MsgReadIndexResp for a forwarded one - from r.raftLog.committed whenever that size test holds, without contacting the quorum; applying a committed change that removes the leading node leaves it leading under the default StepDownOnRemoval=false (raft.go:1985-2012, raft.go:282-287) with a configuration whose only voter is another node, and the write path alone refuses that node's proposals (raft.go:1294-1303). The first execution of the probe (CheckRun c39e3b84d6174ce390e9320c9d2bab1b) parsed all six events without loss and its raw observations match the expectation - event 1: node 1 still StateLeader at term 1 with config voters=(2), singleton true, is_voter false; event 2: node 2 leading at term 2 with committed index 4 while node 1 is at 2; event 3: node 1 answered the read with read_states 1 and read_index 2, emitting no message at all (heartbeats_emitted 0, messages_emitted empty, pending_reads 0); event 4: the same request answered by node 2 returned index 4, covering its commit index; event 5: after three heartbeat intervals with no replies node 1 repeated the same index 2 and was still leading at term 1 - but every comparison verdict came back unknown, with the receipt's own diagnostics ('No corresponding prerequisite events reached', 'No complete applicable result observation'), because the comparison specification used a per-event identity value so no prerequisite event could satisfy the witness identity check. No comparison is therefore completed, and the raw events are not treated as a validated witness for the defect. The corrected specification (shared scenario identity plus a correlated prerequisite chain) is submitted with this update for a fresh execution; until that receipt exists, the safety concern stays asserted on source reasoning and a native draft run.\\\",\n  \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\n   \\\"The raw events of the first receipt are not a completed comparison: the verdicts are unknown because of the comparison wiring, so nothing in this receipt contradicts or confirms the suspicious behaviour, and no failed prerequisite chain was caused by the target.\\\",\n   \\\"A client is expected to direct linearizable reads at the current leader; the library cannot detect staleness in general, so the client-side premise is what the narrow claim rests against.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\n   \\\"The scenario requires the application to apply a committed configuration change that removes the leading node while Config.StepDownOnRemoval is false.\\\",\n   \\\"The removed leader stays at its old term only while nothing from the current configuration carries a higher term to it; with CheckQuorum or PreVote enabled the window is bounded by the next heartbeat exchange.\\\",\n   \\\"The first execution's comparison verdicts are unknown and the corrected basis has not been executed yet; no bound is claimed for how long a client that never retries elsewhere stays exposed.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"knowledge\\\":[\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"9ad1a10e85bb41578fbb8a42a6890ab3-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"IsSingleton is a size-only test over the configuration.\\\"},\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"9ad1a10e85bb41578fbb8a42a6890ab3-knowledge-1\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"StepLeader answers MsgReadIndex locally whenever IsSingleton holds.\\\"},\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"9ad1a10e85bb41578fbb8a42a6890ab3-knowledge-2\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"A removed leader keeps leading by default while its proposals are refused.\\\"}\n  ],\n  \\\"answers\\\":{\n   \\\"9ad1a10e85bb41578fbb8a42a6890ab3-gap-1\\\":{\n    \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The permitted sequence is: two voters {1,2} with node 1 elected leader through a real MsgHup/MsgVote round; the application proposes and then applies the committed change that removes node 1 (ConfChangeRemoveNode node_id=1) on both nodes, which leaves node 1 in StateLeader with config voters=(2) because Config.StepDownOnRemoval defaults to false (receipt c39e3b84d6174ce390e9320c9d2bab1b, parsed event index 1: state StateLeader, term 1, config voters=(2), singleton true, is_voter false). The node that then holds the current commit index is node 2: it campaigns in {2} and commits one entry, so its committed index is 4 while the removed leader is frozen at 2 (parsed event index 2: node 2 StateLeader at term 2, committed_index 4, removed_leader_committed_index 2, actual_leader_ahead true).\\\",\n    \\\"resolved\\\":True}}}]}\nopen('update4.json','w').write(json.dumps(u,indent=2)+\\\"\\\\n\\\")\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_13-42-19-etcd_raft-real-run --submission update4.json 2>&1 | tail -8\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
